      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-4436-2",
        "name": "USN-4436-2",
        "description": "USN-4436-1 fixed a vulnerability in librsvg. The upstream fix caused a regression when parsing certain SVG files. This update backs out the fix pending further investigation.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that librsvg incorrectly handled parsing certain SVG  files. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause librsvg to  crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu  16.04 LTS. (CVE-2017-11464)    It was discovered that librsvg incorrectly handled parsing certain SVG  files with nested patterns. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue  to cause librsvg to consume resources and crash, resulting in a denial of  service. (CVE-2019-20446)",
        "aliases": []
      },
      "timestamp": "2020-07-29T12:43:59Z",
